#------ Input file for system specifications

# USER: 
#    1) The information within this file is meant to allow for the most efficient program run, meaning accurate information is important
#    2) Generally file system block sizes are smaller one personal computers compared to, say, a super/high-performance computer.
#       It is highly recommended to research how to obtain your computers file system block size
#
# NOTE: This file follows a key-value pair. That is, the value is only matched with the key
# eliminating the possibility of incorrect reads due to line dependencies.

FileSystemBlockSize 1024 // Smallest writeable file size on the file system (kilobytes)
AvailableMem        8    // Amount of memory (RAM) allocated to the process (gigabytes)
